{"abstract":"Neural decoding is an important method in cognitive neuroscience that aims to decode brain representations from recorded neural activity using a multivariate machine learning model. The THINGS initiative provides a large EEG dataset of 46 subjects watching rapidly shown images. Here, we test the feasibility of using this method for decoding high-level object features using recent deep learning models. We create a derivative dataset from this of living vs non-living entities test 15 different deep learning models with 5 different architectures and compare to a SOTA linear model. We show that the linear model is not able to solve the decoding task, while almost all the deep learning models are successful, suggesting that in some cases non-linear models are needed to decode neural representations. We also run a comparative study of the models’ performance on individual object categories, and suggest how artificial neural networks can be used to study brain activity.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dixen, Laurits","Heinrich, Stefan","Burelli, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798535"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmark","Deep learning","EEG","Neural decoding","Things"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring deep learning models for eeg neural decoding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105000980847","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798535","identifier":[{"id":"105000980847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-65008d59-2725-4f72-af0d-65781c75a91a"],"keyword":["Benchmark","Deep Learning","EEG","Neural Decoding","THINGS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-542395422C230DF5EB64C8848F0D378D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, brAIn lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurits","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"e20164d2-7e0c-4f05-88be-ca477dfc5f8c","name":"Dixen, Laurits","orcid":"0009-0001-4447-5222","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","locid":"1abda59f-c493-4824-a7b1-7470d66f08d1","name":"Heinrich, Stefan","orcid":"0000-0001-9913-3206","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burelli, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0003-2804-9028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-82487-6_12","isbn":["9783031824869"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"162-175","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"International Symposium on Artificial Intelligence and Neuroscience"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000980847"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-65008d59-2725-4f72-af0d-65781c75a91a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring Deep Learning Models for EEG Neural Decoding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798535","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Accurately quantifying player experience is challenging for many reasons: identifying a ground truth and building validated and reliable scales are both challenging tasks; on top of that, empirical results are often moderated by individual factors. In this study, we investigate the impact of individual differences in the operationalisation of player experience by cross-referencing multiple modalities (i.e. questionnaires, gameplay and heart rate) and identifying the interplay between their scales","author_count":3,"contributors":["Frost Jensen, Maj","Dixen, Laurits","Burelli, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718910"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross referencing modalities","Individual differences","Operationalisation","Player Experience","Quantification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hades again and again a study on frustration tolerance physiology and player experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2401.14878","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-718910","ids":["itu-bdf9b4f9-9914-4dde-9854-7fec5e4d1efd"],"keyword":["Cross-referencing modalities","Individual differences","Operationalisation","Player experience","Quantification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-8726CF0B64FABF54A138175273260310"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100051885/IEEE_COG_2023_Hades.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2401.14878","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Maj","key":"frostjensenpau","last":"Frost Jensen","name":"Frost Jensen, Maj","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurits","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"e20164d2-7e0c-4f05-88be-ca477dfc5f8c","name":"Dixen, Laurits","orcid":"0009-0001-4447-5222","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burelli, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0003-2804-9028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2401.14878","eisbn":["9783031549670"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of ACG 2023","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"14528"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187704008"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bdf9b4f9-9914-4dde-9854-7fec5e4d1efd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hades Again and Again: A Study on Frustration Tolerance, Physiology and Player Experience","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718910","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Videogames have been a catalyst for advances in many research fields, such as artificial intelligence, human-computer interaction, or virtual reality. Over the years, research in fields such as artificial intelligence has enabled the design of new types of games, while games have often served as a powerful tool for testing and simulation. Can this also happen with neuroscience? What is the current relationship between neuroscience and games research? what can we expect from the future? In this article, we’ll try to answer these questions, analysing the current state-of-the-art at the crossroads between neuroscience and games and envisioning future directions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Burelli, Paolo","Dixen, Laurits"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776397"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Accuracy and Precision","Biological system modeling","Games","Neuroimaging","Neuroscience","Solid modeling","Video games"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"playing with neuroscience past present and future of neuroimaging and games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103214159/IEEE_CoG_2024_Playing_with_Neuroscience_Vision_6_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-776397","ids":["itu-488fa670-bbb9-4c1d-9029-414f2f38523c"],"keyword":["Accuracy and Precision","Biological system modeling","Games","Neuroimaging","Neuroscience","Solid modeling","Video games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B266C693F1EF2913833D68F632798692"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103214159/IEEE_CoG_2024_Playing_with_Neuroscience_Vision_6_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, brAIn lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burelli, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0003-2804-9028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurits","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"e20164d2-7e0c-4f05-88be-ca477dfc5f8c","name":"Dixen, Laurits","orcid":"0009-0001-4447-5222","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9798350350678"],"isbn":["9798350350685"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Conference on Games 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203545892"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-488fa670-bbb9-4c1d-9029-414f2f38523c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Playing With Neuroscience: Past, Present and Future of Neuroimaging and Games","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776397","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Uncanny Valley phenomenon refers to the feeling of unease that arises when interacting with characters that appear almost, but not quite, human-like. First theorised by Masahiro Mori in 1970, it has since been widely observed in different contexts from humanoid robots to video games, in which it can result in players feeling uncomfortable or disconnected from the game, leading to a lack of immersion and potentially reducing the overall enjoyment. The phenomenon has been observed and described mostly through behavioural studies based on self-reported scales of uncanny feeling: however, there is still no consensus on its cognitive and perceptual origins, which limits our understanding of its impact on player experience. In this paper, we present a study aimed at identifying the mechanisms that trigger the uncanny response by collecting and analysing both self-reported feedback and EEG data. Index Terms—Uncanny Valley, Virtual Characters, Video Games, EEG, ERP, Survey, Perception, Cognition","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gorlini, Chiara","Dixen, Laurits","Burelli, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718833"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan"],"keyword":["Behavioural Studies","Cognitive Origins","Cognitive and Perceptual Origins","EEG Data","ERP","Human Computer Interaction","Human like Characters","Humanoid robots","Masahiro Mori","Perceptual Mechanisms","Player Feedback","Player Immersion","Self reported Scales","Uncanny Valley","Video Game Experience"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating the uncanny valley phenomenon through the temporal dynamics of neural responses to virtual characters","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100050924/IEEE_COG_2023_Uncanny_Valley_EEG_3_.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718833","identifier":[{"id":"85180556743","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1c828948-693c-48e1-aaff-83894a1b75f7"],"keyword":["Behavioural Studies","Cognitive Origins","Cognitive and Perceptual Origins","EEG Data","ERP","Human-Computer Interaction","Human-like Characters","Humanoid Robots","Masahiro Mori","Perceptual Mechanisms","Player Feedback","Player Immersion","Self-reported Scales","Uncanny Valley","Video Game Experience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A9EA8DEE3F1264E7A6E2A6E81B60D54"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100050924/IEEE_COG_2023_Uncanny_Valley_EEG_3_.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiara","key":"gorlinipau","last":"Gorlini","name":"Gorlini, Chiara","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurits","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"e20164d2-7e0c-4f05-88be-ca477dfc5f8c","name":"Dixen, Laurits","orcid":"0009-0001-4447-5222","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burelli, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0003-2804-9028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cog57401.2023.10333130","eisbn":["9798350322774"],"isbn":["9798350322781"],"publisher":"IEEE","series":"Proceedings of the 2023 IEEE conference on Games","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Game"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180556743"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1c828948-693c-48e1-aaff-83894a1b75f7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigating the Uncanny Valley Phenomenon Through the Temporal Dynamics of Neural Responses to Virtual Characters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718833","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Game difficulty is a crucial aspect of game design, that can be directly influenced by tweaking game mechanics. Perceived difficulty can however also be influenced by simply altering the graphics to something more threatening. Here, we present a study with 12 participants playing 4 different minigames with either altered graphics or mechanics to make the game more difficult. Using EEG bandpower analysis, we find that frontal lobe activity was heightened in all 4 of the mechanically challenging versions and in 2/4 of the visually altered versions, all differences that did not emerge from the self-reported player experience. This suggests that EEG could researchers with a more sensitive tool for investigating challenge in games.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hegedues, Christine","Dias Constantino, João Pedro","Dixen, Laurits","Burelli, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718916"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Challenge Measurement","EEG Bandpower Analysis","Frontal Lobe Activity","Game Difficulty","Game Mechanics","Game design","Neurogaming Research","Perceived Difficulty","Player Experience","Visual Alterations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating perceived and mechanical challenge in games through cognitive activity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100051620/IEEE_COG_2023_Hades_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-718916","identifier":[{"id":"85180549906","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c7a73d9d-2dcd-4cbb-86e7-76b0639a56a4"],"keyword":["Challenge Measurement","EEG Bandpower Analysis","Frontal Lobe Activity","Game Design","Game Difficulty","Game Mechanics","Neurogaming Research","Perceived Difficulty","Player Experience","Visual Alterations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A41B198D57540787FAD3E3FA805C88F4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100051620/IEEE_COG_2023_Hades_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine","key":"hegeduespau","last":"Hegedues","name":"Hegedues, Christine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"João Pedro","key":"diasconstantinopau","last":"Dias Constantino","name":"Dias Constantino, João Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurits","key":"dixenpau","last":"Dixen","locid":"e20164d2-7e0c-4f05-88be-ca477dfc5f8c","name":"Dixen, Laurits","orcid":"0009-0001-4447-5222","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burelli, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0003-2804-9028","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cog57401.2023.10333149","eisbn":["9798350322774"],"isbn":["9798350322781"],"publisher":"IEEE","series":"Proceedings of the 2023 IEEE conference on Games","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Game"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180549906"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"s